Leo: That sounds great. I''ve heard they are showing some famous ink paintings.
Mia: Yes, and there are some of Van Gogh''s works on display too.
Leo: Wonderful! What time should we go?
Mia: Let''s go in the morning. It''s usually quieter, so we can look at every detail.
Leo: Good idea. Should we ask Anna to come with us?
Mia: Of course. She loves painting, and she''s hoping to become an artist one day.
Leo: Perfect. I''ll check the website to see which artworks are on display.
Mia: Thanks. Remember, we are not allowed to touch any of the paintings.
Leo: I know. But we can take a few photos and buy some postcards to bring home.', 'Mia 想周六去新的艺术馆;Leo 说那里在展出著名水墨画,还有梵高的作品;两人决定上午去,因为人少、能看清细节;还要叫热爱绘画、想当艺术家的 Anna 一起;Leo 去查网站看展品;Mia 提醒不能触碰画作,但能拍照、买明信片。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When do Mia and Leo decide to visit the museum?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["On Saturday morning.","On Sunday evening.","On Friday afternoon.","On Monday night."]},{"q":"Why do they choose to go in the morning?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It is cheaper in the morning.","It is usually quieter then.","The museum closes at noon.","The paintings look brighter then."]},{"q":"Why do they want Anna to join them?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She loves painting and hopes to be an artist.","She works at the museum.","She has a free ticket.","She has a car to drive them."]},{"q":"What will Leo do before the trip?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Buy lunch for everyone.","Check the website for the artworks on display.","Paint a picture of the museum.","Call the museum guide."]},{"q":"What are visitors not allowed to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Take any photos.","Buy postcards.","Touch any of the paintings.","Speak to each other."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U2', 'sufe');
Sophie: Yes! Our group is preparing a guessing game about famous artists.
Tom: That sounds fun. How does the game work?
Sophie: Each group gives five clues about an artist without saying the name. Then the others guess.
Tom: Clever. Which artist did your group choose?
Sophie: Qi Baishi. We''ll say he painted shrimps and flowers in a fresh and lively manner.
Tom: Nice clues. My group is going to display our own paintings in the main hall.
Sophie: Wonderful. The teacher told us to put our best works on display by Friday.
Tom: I''d better hurry, then. I still want to finish my landscape before the show.
Sophie: Good luck! I''m sure the whole school will enjoy the festival.', 'Tom 问 Sophie 是否参加下周的校园艺术节;Sophie 说她们组在准备「猜艺术家」游戏:每组给五条线索但不说名字,别人来猜;她们选了齐白石,会说他以清新生动的方式画虾和花;Tom 组要在大厅展出自画;老师让大家周五前把最好的作品摆出来;Tom 想在展览前画完风景画;Sophie 祝他好运,相信全校都会喜欢艺术节。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Sophie''s group preparing for the festival?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A guessing game about famous artists.","A singing competition.","A cooking show.","A sports match."]},{"q":"How does the guessing game work?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Players draw pictures very quickly.","Each group gives five clues without saying the artist''s name.","Players sing songs by famous artists.","Each group writes a long essay."]},{"q":"Which artist did Sophie''s group choose?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Van Gogh.","Bob Dylan.","Qi Baishi.","Shakespeare."]},{"q":"What is Tom''s group going to do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Play music on the stage.","Sell postcards to visitors.","Guess the artists first.","Display their own paintings in the main hall."]},{"q":"What does Tom still want to do before the show?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Finish his landscape painting.","Buy a new brush.","Choose a different artist.","Write the five clues."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U2', 'sufe');
Emma: That''s great, Ben! What made you want to start?
Ben: I love the songs of Bob Dylan, and I want to play them myself.
Emma: He''s a wonderful songwriter. Did you know he won the Nobel Prize for Literature?
Ben: Yes, the first songwriter ever to get it. His words are like poems.
Emma: They are. At first the guitar will be hard, so don''t give up too soon.
Ben: I won''t. My teacher told me to practise a little every day.
Emma: That''s good advice. Even great musicians had to start with simple songs.
Ben: Right. One day I hope to perform on a real stage in front of an audience.
Emma: I''m sure you will. Keep going, and I''ll come to your first concert!', 'Ben 决定今年学吉他;Emma 问原因;Ben 说他爱鲍勃·迪伦的歌、想自己弹;Emma 说迪伦是了不起的词曲作者,还获了诺贝尔文学奖;Ben 说他是首位获此奖的词曲作者,歌词像诗;Emma 提醒吉他起初难、别太快放弃;Ben 说老师让他每天练一点;Emma 说大音乐家也从简单歌曲起步;Ben 希望有一天能在真正的舞台上对观众演奏;Emma 说一定会去听他的首场音乐会。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What has Ben decided to do this year?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Learn to paint.","Write a book.","Learn to play the guitar.","Join a dance club."]},{"q":"Why does Ben want to learn it?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["His parents asked him to.","He wants to win a prize.","His friends all play it.","He loves Bob Dylan''s songs and wants to play them."]},{"q":"What did Emma say about Bob Dylan?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He won the Nobel Prize for Literature.","He never wrote his own songs.","He stopped singing long ago.","He was a famous painter."]},{"q":"What advice did Ben''s teacher give him?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Buy a very expensive guitar.","Practise a little every day.","Play only difficult songs.","Stop after one week."]},{"q":"What does Ben hope to do one day?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Sell his guitar.","Become a painter instead.","Perform on a real stage in front of an audience.","Teach at a university."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U2', 'sufe');

